    "collapsible_content_WCcf7h": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_xFKa7f": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What vehicles does MoonShade work with?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonShade works on most SUVs, crossovers, mid-size and full-size trucks, Jeeps, RVs, and lightweight trailers — anything with a smooth exterior surface and roughly 7 feet of mounting span. Moon-confirmed vehicles include the Jeep Wrangler, Toyota 4Runner, Ford Bronco, Subaru Outback, Toyota Tacoma, Ford F-150, and Airstream Basecamp, among many others. See the <a href=\"/pages/vehicle-compatibility-list\" title=\"Vehicle Compatibility List\">full list</a> here.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_8JAGdm": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does MoonShade need a roof rack?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>No. MoonShade attaches via MoonAnchors — suction, magnetic, or surface-mount depending on your vehicle. No roof rack, no drilling, no permanent modification.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_iLxTyq": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does setup take?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>About 5 minutes, solo. One person, no tools.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_N9Q4UG": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How much does MoonShade weigh?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>8 lbs. It packs to 36 × 6 inches — fits under the back seat of most vehicles.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_VQigf6": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How does MoonShade hold up in wind?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonShade is rated to 30 mph and includes guy lines and tensioners for added stability. In practice, owners regularly report it holding through stronger gusts — one rode out 30–40 mph winds in Nevada without issue. For high-wind conditions, stake out all four guy lines and keep support poles at a lower height.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_PRUkhX": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What do people use MoonShade for?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Sun protection is the most common use — mentioned in over 275 reviews. Rain coverage, outdoor cooking, boondocking shade, tailgating, beach days, and backyard gatherings all come up regularly.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_rqYVkH": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How is MoonShade different from a roof rack awning?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Roof rack awnings are fixed to one vehicle and require a rack to mount. The awning itself typically runs $400–$1,200+, with professional installation an added cost on top of that. MoonShade attaches to almost any vehicle without a rack, permanent hardware, or installation — it weighs 8 lbs and packs into a bag.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
